<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Autonomous Governorate of Estonia</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1918 CE · capital Reval</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Self-governing Estonian province created by Russia's Provisional Government in 1917, whose assembly prepared the declaration of Estonian independence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia's</a> Provisional Government decreed on 12 April 1917 that the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/governorate-of-estonia">Governorate of Estonia</a> would be joined with the Estonian-speaking northern districts of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/governorate-of-livonia">Governorate of Livonia</a>, uniting the Estonian people in one autonomous province. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaan-poska">Jaan Poska</a>, mayor of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a>, became its commissar.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>For the first time <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a> governed their own land. An elected provincial assembly, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonian-provincial-assembly">Maapäev</a>, met in July 1917, and a Provincial Government led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-pats">Konstantin Päts</a> was formed. Estonian replaced German as the language of administration, and national regiments were organised.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Bolshevik coup, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonian-provincial-assembly">Maapäev</a> declared itself the sovereign power in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a> on 28 November 1917 before being dispersed by local Bolsheviks. As German troops advanced and the Bolsheviks withdrew, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonian-salvation-committee">Salvation Committee</a> declared the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> on 24 February 1918; the Germans then occupied the country until November.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/autonomous-governorate-of-estonia.jpg" alt="Autonomous Governorate of Estonia" width="320" height="204"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: SKopp, PeepP and ‍others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Estonia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Reval</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jaan Poska, Konstantin Päts</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Autonomous Estonia, Estonian Autonomous Governorate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=autonomous-governorate-of-estonia" aria-label="Autonomous Governorate of Estonia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5201 181 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Autonomous Governorate of Estonia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5521 437L5521 437M5521 437L5635 424M5521 437L5521 437"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 437h0M5635 424h0M5521 437h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5521 437h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5521 437h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=autonomous-governorate-of-estonia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
